   "notes": "Static-lattice 0 K DFT parameterization of the ideal cubic Pm-3m (Glazer a0a0a0) CaSiO3 perovskite branch. The paper finds this branch dynamically unstable at all investigated pressures, so this is a theoretical reference curve and not a stable ambient phase. Table 2 reports V0/Z; Pm-3m has Z=1, so 44.579 A^3 is also the conventional cubic-cell volume (a0=3.54577 A). All three BM3 coefficients were fitted; no parameter uncertainties, covariance, fit weights, or underlying E(V) rows are published. The Table 2 footnote estimates calculation uncertainty as about 20 meV per molecule, an energy-scale estimate rather than an EOS-coefficient error. The same calculations also have a distinct Pm-3m BM4 fit (V0=44.588 A^3, K0=248 GPa, K0'=4.206, K0''=-0.002 GPa^-1); it is audit metadata rather than a duplicate of this record. The source's nine low-symmetry BM3/BM4 pairs describe different crystallographic phases and must not be attached to this cubic material.",
